-- An exported rule whose input has no written type. The checker infers it from
-- how the rule uses it: handed to a helper that takes a DEONTIC, it is a DEONTIC,
-- and a request has no JSON form for one, so `l4 check` and `l4 batch` refuse it.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF `deliver goods`, `pay invoice`

GIVEN duty IS A DEONTIC Person Action
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`already fulfilled` duty MEANS
  CONSIDER duty
  WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
  OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Is a duty already fulfilled
GIVEN `the duty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is it fulfilled` `the duty` MEANS `already fulfilled` `the duty`
